Joan appetize new film starring Pete  Davidson has just been released on  demand which lists itself as a  semi-autobiographical film about  Davidson's life the guy is only 26 and  already has a movie about his life so I  wanted to dig a little deeper into the  king of Staten Island and find out what  in this movie is real and what is not so  buckle in because here we go  Pete Davidson plays Scott the same name  of his real-life father and to whom the  film is dedicated in the film Scott's  father was a firefighter who tragically  died when a building he was trying to  put out collapsed in real life Pete's  father was also a firefighter who died  during the September 11th attacks he was  last seen running up the stairs of the  Marriot World Trade Center before it  collapsed Pete was 7 when this happened  just like Scott's character in the film  and Scott was only seven when it  happened so Pete has also used tattoos  to remember his father and tattoos play  an important role in the film with his  character even wanting to open a tattoo  parlor restaurant website body art  guru.com has a great article outlining  the meaning of all of his tattoos which  I'll leave in the description below  including an ID card of his father his  father's initials SMD his father's  fireman's hat and the number 11 which  some have speculated stands for the date  his father died there's even a scene  where all the firefighters sing The  Wallflowers of one headlight which Pete  says was one of his father's favorite  songs  another interesting addition to the cast  with real-life connections was the  addition of Steve Buscemi as a  firefighter many of you may not know  that Buscemi was an actual New York City  firefighter from 1980 to 1984 and during  the September 11th attacks he  volunteered at his old Engine Company  digging through the rubble looking for  missing firefighters Pete's father's  death resulted in him lashing out at  school and he even considered suicide in  his youth something that is briefly  touched upon in the opening scene of the  film where his character closes his eyes  going down the freeway and nearly  crashes PETA said that the music of Kid  Cudi saved his life and if you pay close  attention both the beginning and end of  the movies start with songs from Kid  Cudi the beginning featuring a song  titled just what I am and the end  pursuit of happiness  Crohn's disease is also a significant  part of Scott's life in the film much  like it is in Pete's in his late teens  Pete was diagnosed with the disease and  used marijuana to help them through the  pain among other things the film  portrays the character of Scott as a  pothead and part of Pete's SNL persona  is that of one too and his latest  stand-up special he even talks about how  louis c.k almost got him fired from SNL  when he found him smoking pot in his  dressing room unlike the film however  real-life Pete Davidson has a history of  dating some well-known celebs including  Kate Beckinsale Margaret quale and  Ariana Grande all of these relationships  lasted relatively short and in the film  he talks about his relationship with the  character of Kelsey not working because  of his mental health there's like  something wrong with me in 2017 Pete was  diagnosed with borderline personality  disorder a disorder which according to  the Mayo Clinic can include patterns of  unstable intense relationships the film  also highlights the relationship between  Scott and his mother Margie played by  Marissa Tomei both his movie and  real-life mom in real life she's called  Amy are nurses and Pete has said he's  felt guilty about his mom not dating  much because she was focused on raising  the kids and yes Pete also has a  real-life sister but unlike her being  called Claire her real-life name is  Casey fun fact Claire is played by Maude  Apatow director Judd Apatow's daughter  in preparation for writing the script  Judd Apatow spent a lot of time  interviewing Pete's family and friends  in fact Pete's actual grandpa has a  brief cameo in the film although the  character of Scott in the film is  portrayed as a lazy and lost millennial  real-life Pete was motivated and  hard-working  Pete started comedy at the age of 15 and  was quite ambitious eventually getting a  small role in Apatow strain wreck where  Bill Hader referred him to Lorne  Michaels to audition for Saturday Night  Live the film is also riddled with  personal friends of Davidson's like a  Ricky Velez who plays Oscar and the  co-writer of the film is his best friend  Dave cirrus not to mention some of the  firefighters in the firefighter scenes  are actual men and women who served  along Pete's own father  overall the king of Staten Island is  pretty true to Pete Davidson as a person  but the plot around his character is  fictionalized  as a patel was said this is a movie  about Pete Davidson if he never pursued  comedy Apatow has a history of mining  comedic talent and highlighting their  personal stories it will be interesting  to see what or who he chooses to focus  on next thanks for watching everyone be  sure to LIKE and subscribe I'm always  coming up with new and interesting  videos for more bad takes follow me on  twitter at big story whitey until next  time remember daddy loves you very much
 

